truthtable rows </span></a><u></u><u></u></span></p></div><table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"100%\" style=\"width:100.0%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:solid lightgrey 1.0pt;background:white;padding:7.5pt 11.25pt 7.5pt 11.25pt\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#b1b0b0\">Sarah Wang &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sarah...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Mar 20 10:08PM -0700 </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#2e2e2e\"><br><br>Hi Adrian, <br>I am running an analysis and the truthtable is showing some strange things. <br>I have attached the raw data and R codes that I have used. <br> <br>My questions are: <br>1. why does the truthtable row 44 show KOR OUT is 1 while the data show KOR <br>is out of the set?<br>2. why does truthtable row 18 show USA OUT is 0 while the data show USA is <br>in the set?<br>3. More importantly, is there anything alarming that I should be aware of? <br>4. Could you please also suggest the way to resolve this? (I know how to <br>manually change the OUT from 0 to 1 or vice versa in R. Is there any other <br>way to achieve it? )<br> <br>Thank you in advance <br>Kind regards<br> <br>Sarah<u></u><u></u></span></p></td></tr></table><div style=\"margin-top:3.75pt;margin-bottom:30.0pt\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:whitesmoke\"><span style=\"font-size:8.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><a href=\"#m_-2132828654774547874_digest_top\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\">Back to top</span></a> <u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div><div><table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"100%\" style=\"width:100.0%\"><tr><td style=\"padding:3.0pt 0cm 0cm 0cm\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:8.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#636363\">You received this digest because you&#39;re subscribed to 